// Test: bugfixes/codegen_stack_remaining_cross_class_void_from_method_body
// Grammar: static_method_call → ClassName.method(args)  (grammar.ebnf §5
//   static_method_call) where the *receiver class* of the call is a DIFFERENT
//   user-defined class than the one whose method body contains the call, and
//   the resolved static method has a void return type. Surfaces as
//   `MethodCall { receiver: Variable("OtherClass"), method }` in HIR.
// Regression: CODEGEN_STACK_REMAINING (dashboard fp ab7f9b3f, first reported
//   in 0.30.268 against Clean Studio's 15 logic-class entrypoint).
//   Three earlier fixes (618571c5, 06e6cd9c, 1cffab2d) shipped between
//   0.30.307 and 0.30.310 each closed *one* angle of the bug but left this
//   case open. Confirmed by the dashboard re-report on 0.30.310:
//   "bytes near offset still show call followed by drop with no push
//   between them".
//
//   Two compounding root causes:
//
//   1. Resolver ordering: the resolver processes classes sequentially via
//      `resolve_class`. Class A's method bodies are resolved BEFORE class B's
//      method symbols are registered (B's `SymbolKind::Class.methods` list
//      is still empty during A's Pass 2). When A's body contains
//      `B.bar(args)` — parsed as `MethodCall { receiver: Variable("B") }`
//      and routed through `resolve_method_call_expression`'s class-receiver
//      shortcut at line 2046 — `lookup_class_member(B_id, "bar")` returns
//      None and the call is lowered as a `ResolvedHirExpression::StaticMethodCall`
//      with `method_symbol_id = SymbolId(0)`. MIR codegen then emits it as
//      `MirOperand::NamedFunction { name: "B.bar", symbol_id: 0 }`.
//
//   2. Codegen void-detection gap: the dest=None Drop decision in
//      `generate_call_instruction` cannot prove void via signature
//      (SymbolId 0 ⇒ no entry in `function_signatures`), via the hardcoded
//      builtin list ("B.bar" ≠ "print" et al.), via the plugin-bridge
//      `function_return_types` map (B is not a plugin), or via the WASM-
//      level last-resort `wasm_function_is_void` (which only sees functions
//      that have already been *emitted*, but `start:` is generated before
//      `B.bar` itself). All four checks fall through → spurious `drop` →
//      wasmparser reports "expected a type but nothing on stack".
//
//   Fix: in `mir_codegen::generate()`, seed `function_return_types` (a
//   name-keyed registry already used for plugin-bridge void detection)
//   with every entry from `mir_program.functions` before the first
//   function is generated. The dest=None Drop decision now treats both
//   `MirType::Void` and `MirType::Ptr(Void)` (the canonical lowering of
//   `ConcreteType::Null`) as void, and strips the leading qualifier so
//   "B.bar" resolves to the bare "bar" entry. The codegen path no longer
//   depends on resolver method-symbol resolution succeeding, so the
//   resolver ordering issue stops mattering for void detection.
//
//   Tests the failing pattern minimally: 2 classes, 1 void method each,
//   class A's method body invokes class B's void method as an
//   expression-statement. Was the bare minimum case to reproduce the
//   "call · drop" emission Clean Studio observed at scale across 15
//   logic classes.
//
// Expected output:
//   from B
//   from A
//   done

start:
	A.foo("from A")
	print("done")

class A
	functions:
		foo(string s)
			B.bar("from B")
			print(s)

class B
	functions:
		bar(string s)
			print(s)
